{
  "format": "call-of-slop-construct-part/1",
  "name": "Shredder Block",
  "description": "Weld it on a Breaker Core's +x side, or beside another Shredder Block: the Core splits its blocks into squares, each one shredder with a pair of toothed rotors, and its mouth is the whole bed: a wreck whose middle lands over any square is taken in. Each block of an n x n square adds 1 + n/4 to the Core's rate (a lone block 1.25, a 3 x 3's 1.75 each), so bigger squares pay more. A wrecked block keeps its square and adds nothing until mended. No power of its own: the Core draws a share for it. The rotors hurt: keep clear while it works.",
